==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[n-]]

===Etymology===
{{proto|Germanic|ne|not|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|ne|no, not|lang=}}. Akin to {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|ne||not|lang=ang}}

===Prefix===
{{head|ang|prefix|cat=prefixes|head=ne-}}

# not, usually syncopated to n-
#: ''{{term|neom||am not|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|næs||was not|lang=ang}}; {{term|næron|nǣron|were not|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nic||not I|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nænig|nǣniġ|no one, none, not any, no (adj.)|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nealles||not at all, by no means|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nefne||unless, except, not even|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nabban||to have not, be without|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nagan|nāgan|to not owe, not own|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|næfre|nǣfre|never|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nyllan||will not, wish not, be unwilling, refuse|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nat|nāt|[I] do not know|lang=ang}}, from {{term|nytan||to know not|lang=ang}}''
#: ''{{term|nyten||ignorant|lang=ang}} (from ne + witan)''

